config XIAOMI_MCA_CORE
	tristate "Annibale MCA common helpers (experimental)"
	depends on EXPERT && OF && MI_HARDWARE_ID
	help
	  Build the MCA device-tree parser, hardware identity and workqueue.
	  These are common helpers, not a battery supply or charging policy.
	  Leave disabled until the remaining Annibale charging stack is ready.

config XIAOMI_MCA_GLINK
	tristate "Annibale MCA ADSP transport (experimental)"
	depends on XIAOMI_MCA_CORE && QTI_PMIC_GLINK
	depends on QTI_BATTERY_CHARGER=n
	help
	  Build the two-owner MCA charging/auxiliary PMIC Glink transport.
	  This occupies the same owners as the standard battery charger client.
	  It must not be selected alongside that client. No charging strategy
	  or current/voltage policy is enabled by this transport alone.

config XIAOMI_MCA_SERVICES
	tristate "Annibale MCA charging and fuel-gauge interfaces (experimental)"
	depends on XIAOMI_MCA_CORE && SYSFS
	help
	  Build the xm_power sysfs namespace, event notifications, charging
	  control dispatcher and fuel-gauge callback registry. These require
	  real hardware/policy providers; missing operations return errors.
	  No battery power-supply driver or charging policy is supplied here.

config XIAOMI_MCA_BQ27Z561
	tristate "Annibale BQ27Z561 read-only telemetry (experimental)"
	depends on XIAOMI_MCA_SERVICES && I2C
	help
	  Read standard gauge registers on the Annibale master gauge at 0x55.
	  Publish measured values through MCA and read-only I2C device sysfs.
	  No battery power_supply, polling, firmware writes or charging policy.
	  Do not load alongside the stock gauge driver. Leave disabled outside
	  explicit development builds until pack variants are tested on hardware.
